      {
        "id": 238259,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-06-07T14:53:26.177Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Another similarly weird “I don’t actually care” ship for me:  Tachyon and Absolute Zero.  Not at all based on their personalities, but simply on the fact that cryogenic temperatures + electricity = superconduction, aka speed.  (A little backwards, since Tachy uses speed to generate electricity, but it’s close enough to amuse me.)</p>\n<p>I imagine Tachy working late at night on some thorny scientific problem, while Ryan looks on from his cryo-suite, and Tachy going “I’m not fast enough, I need to speed up the electrons in my brain”, and Ryan says something about how depressed he is that nobody can ever touch him, and then Tachy gets a cartoon lightbulb above her head.  The rest writes itself.</p>",
